1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:07,528
Coding agents, explained: you would never fix your car with the mechanic on the phone, but that is how you use an AI chatbot.

2
00:00:08,028 --> 00:00:10,392
A chat assistant is the mechanic on the phone.

3
00:00:10,692 --> 00:00:11,787
He can only talk.

4
00:00:12,087 --> 00:00:16,295
So you paste his fix into your code, run it, and carry the error back to him.

5
00:00:16,595 --> 00:00:17,490
Again and again.

6
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:22,208
A coding agent is the mechanic standing in your garage, with tools.

7
00:00:22,508 --> 00:00:25,274
You give it one job, in your terminal or your editor.

8
00:00:25,574 --> 00:00:26,660
Then it works in a loop.

9
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,097
It reads your files.

10
00:00:28,397 --> 00:00:29,371
It edits the code.

11
00:00:29,671 --> 00:00:31,519
It runs a command, and checks the result.

12
00:00:31,819 --> 00:00:32,682
Still broken?

13
00:00:32,982 --> 00:00:35,457
It goes around again, until the job is done.

14
00:00:35,757 --> 00:00:39,127
That whole visit, every step and every result, is one session.

15
00:00:39,627 --> 00:00:41,050
You stop being the messenger.

16
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:43,428
You watch, and you can stop it at any moment.

17
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:46,806
It can still be wrong, so give it a test to run.

18
00:00:47,106 --> 00:00:48,343
But notice what changed.

19
00:00:48,643 --> 00:00:50,523
The mechanic did not get a bigger brain.

20
00:00:50,823 --> 00:00:53,196
He got hands, and a way to check his own work.

21
00:00:53,496 --> 00:00:55,060
That is what makes it an agent.

22
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:56,962
Subscribe for the next one.
